itle loan, personal loan, or advance loan", "Prepaid card", "Student loan", "Vehicle loan or lease"], "keywords": ["misled", "misleading", "deceptive", "lied", "false advertising", "hidden fee", "bait and switch", "unfair", "not disclosed", "promised", "account closed without notice", "frozen account", "funds held", "customer service", "bonus not paid"], "rules": ["An act is unfair if it causes or is likely to cause substantial injury that consumers cannot reasonably avoid and that is not outweighed by benefits to consumers or competition.", "An act is deceptive if it misleads or is likely to mislead a consumer acting reasonably, about something material.", "An act is abusive if it materially interferes with a consumer's ability to understand a term, or takes unreasonable advantage of the consumer's lack of understanding, inability to protect their interests, or reasonable reliance on the company.", "UDAAP is a general standard. It applies when no more specific rule covers the conduct, for example misleading marketing, undisclosed fees, or freezing a consumer's funds without explanation."]}, {"id": "DEPOSITS", "name": "Deposit account rules: Truth in Savings (Regulation DD) and Expedited Funds Availability (Regulation CC)", "citation": "12 CFR 1030; 12 CFR 229", "products": ["Checking or savings account"], "keywords": ["checking", "savings", "deposit", "hold", "funds availability", "check hold", "mobile deposit", "account fee", "maintenance fee", "overdraft fee", "nsf", "interest", "apy", "account closed", "cd", "certificate of deposit"], "rules": ["Regulation DD, 12 CFR 1030.4-1030.5: the institution must disclose fees, the annual percentage yield and account terms before an account is opened, and give 30 days' advance notice of a change that hurts the consumer.", "Regulation DD, 12 CFR 1030.8: advertising may not be misleading or inaccurate, and an account may not be called 'free' if it carries a maintenance or activity fee.", "Regulation CC, 12 CFR 229.10-229.12: